# No Cursor Attribution

Never reference Cursor (or any AI assistant) in anything that lands in the repo.

Strip it from:
- Code comments
- Commit messages and trailers
- PR/issue titles and descriptions
- Code review comments

Specifically, never emit:
- `Co-authored-by: Cursor ...` (or any AI co-author trailer)
- `🤖 Generated with Cursor`, "Generated by Cursor", "via Cursor", etc.
- Comments like `// added by Cursor` or `# Cursor: ...`

```text
# ❌ BAD (commit trailer)
fix(api): handle null node id

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursor@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
fix(api): handle null node id
```

```python
# ❌ BAD
result = probe()  # Cursor: refactored to async

# ✅ GOOD
result = probe()
```

Write comments and messages as if authored by the human committer. No exceptions.
